{"title":"1985 USAMO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/5/8859dbfb7a9ec734e16f2a88fb5cf1104eb6a39b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B,C,D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" /> denote four points in space such that at most one of the distances <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/f/a0fc59c4f526997a9eeacefd898a49672ea95c0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB,AC,AD,BC,BD,CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"215\" height=\"18\" /> is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Determine the maximum value of the sum of the six distances.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is the length that is more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Let spheres with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> around <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/b/f4b521125dee0cf0ad97dc4e77d84073d8644984.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/a/b3a286c25a92cb61f50bcbb54aba01f969a1816d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> must be in the intersection of these spheres, and they must be on the circle created by the intersection to maximize the distance. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/9/a297fbabbe62bb6702fabd74c945022d017268e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC + BC + AD + BD = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"218\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>In fact, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> must be a diameter of the circle. This maximizes the five lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/a/d4ad0ca46478a16fbb3bfb9642319ae51c2c6da9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACBD$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> is a rhombus. \n</p><p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/d/73d7c1d0068b0091f103af52dcd23df707813cb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CAD = 2\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"101\" height=\"14\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/6/4e6dea8420021e3a108370ed3df2a74e53974947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB + CD = 2\\sin{\\theta} + 2\\cos{\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"224\" height=\"16\" />. To maximize this, we must maximize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/5/a75dc122ca8890ce64f66405ede986f3992a6e86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{\\theta} + \\cos{\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" /> on the range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/5/465a8fb599a97128b9f411a55f6e19b801cf7ea5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7dfa8a2a90d521b2b03f5b82a1fb9f85dce88c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />. However, note that we really only have to solve this problem on the range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/5/465a8fb599a97128b9f411a55f6e19b801cf7ea5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/1/821d3f11ab7a3e93c7a404a34224228f0449505a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/7/937be83ecf2e2f0238994a0b9d538f60e179e3df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta &gt; 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" /> is just a symmetrical function.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/d/64db3c5dff3c3e05f0d9893174ef7927efc31c5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta &lt; 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/0/f30690f2f947947268144c5e1f10658023a949b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{\\theta} \\leq \\cos{\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"97\" height=\"17\" />. We know that the derivative of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/1/3b144c5e51935c5f3229f9dced73af7a45486041.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/2/c72d3f209ec3895bcf546050ea1526fbb1aaf661.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{\\theta}$\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" />, and the derivative of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/2/c72d3f209ec3895bcf546050ea1526fbb1aaf661.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{\\theta}$\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/6/0c64a650e96692bfee8d70a6ee12e899723bab2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\sin{\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"16\" />. Thus, the derivative of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/5/a75dc122ca8890ce64f66405ede986f3992a6e86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{\\theta} + \\cos{\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/a/a1a659f1fc81da7f3beba4a296542dfee4656d85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{\\theta} - \\sin{\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" />, which is nonnegative between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/5/465a8fb599a97128b9f411a55f6e19b801cf7ea5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/1/821d3f11ab7a3e93c7a404a34224228f0449505a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, we can conclude that this is an increasing function on this range. \n</p><p>It must be true that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/7/fe7a7260f815ebb2c830a83ae842e726fd4d19bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sin{\\theta} \\leq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"82\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/5/5d575fb144273ad305999bf93d1908c50c8db673.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta \\leq 30^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" />. But, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/5/a75dc122ca8890ce64f66405ede986f3992a6e86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{\\theta} + \\cos{\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" /> is increasing, it is maximized at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/7/52732d97088478d539afaa1d2af75c1b1a2291a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = 30^{\\circ}$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/b/b9bf411f176a26581abebdc3f4a8c78dffb5f47b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = \\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"79\" height=\"21\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/7/81729cf4848260b6feda8ea5ae3f1d0867c890eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />, and our sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/8/bc89142c11a8303fd8788bc2b6016eeff5702d19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 + \\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>~mathboy100\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_USAMO\" title=\"1985 USAMO\">1985 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1985 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1985\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1985 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1985 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1985 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1985 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1985 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1985 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017175317\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.035 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.057 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 267/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1267/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8009/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.484      1 -total\n 50.08%    7.253      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n 47.87%    6.933      1 Template:USAMO_b